[{"id":"xhigh__hf-model-inference/event-0011/reasoning","type":"reasoning","content":"External binding works (172.17.0.2:5000 returns 200). `ps` isn't installed, but I can verify the process via /proc.\n\n\n\nExternal binding works. `ps` isn't available, so I'll confirm the process via /proc.\n\n","source":{"event_id":"event-0011","field":"thought"}},{"id":"xhigh__hf-model-inference/event-0011/action-1","type":"action","content":{"tool_name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"ls -d /proc/114 && cat /proc/114/cmdline | tr '\\0' ' ' && echo && tail -5 /app/service.log","i":"Confirm service process alive and check log"}},"source":{"event_id":"event-0011","field":"tool_calls[0]","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8de6e65603a164c6@55:2"}},{"id":"xhigh__hf-model-inference/event-0011/observation-1","type":"observation","content":{"raw":"/proc/114\n\n127.0.0.1 - - [20/Aug/2026 06:39:02] \"POST /sentiment HTTP/1.1\" 400 -\n127.0.0.1 - - [20/Aug/2026 06:39:02] \"POST /sentiment HTTP/1.1\" 400 -\n127.0.0.1 - - [20/Aug/2026 06:39:02] \"POST /sentiment HTTP/1.1\" 400 -\n127.0.0.1 - - [20/Aug/2026 06:39:08] \"POST /sentiment HTTP/1.1\" 400 -\n172.17.0.2 - - [20/Aug/2026 06:39:14] \"POST /sentiment HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n\n\nWall time: 0.00 seconds","is_error":false,"source_line":58},"source":{"event_id":"event-0011","field":"tool_calls[0].observation","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8de6e65603a164c6@55:2"}},{"id":"xhigh__hf-model-inference/event-0012/reasoning","type":"reasoning","content":"Process 114 is running (cmdline was output, but the output of tr is empty — actually, it's possible that the output of `cat /proc/114/cmdline` got mixed in weirdly. The output of `ls -d /proc/114` is shown, and then the log tail is displayed. The cmdline output appears to be empty between the two, but the process exists and is handling requests, so no problem.\n\nAll verified:\n1. ✅ Model downloaded to /app/model_cache/sentiment_model\n2. ✅ Flask API at POST /sentiment that accepts {\"text\": \"...\"}\n3. ✅ Returns sentiment (positive/negative) and confidence scores in JSON\n4. ✅ Running on 0.0.0.0:5000 (verified via container IP)\n5. ✅ Running in background (nohup, pid 114)\n6. ✅ Error responses return 400 and {\"error\": ...}\n\nOne more consideration: should the service survive even if the session ends? nohup + backgrounding from bash — the process is detached (nohup ignores SIGHUP, and the output is redirected to a file). It should persist inside the container.\n\nAll done. Task complete.\n\n\n\nAll checks pass. The task is complete:\n\n**1. Model downloaded** — `distilbert-base-uncased-finetuned-sst-2-english` saved to `/app/model_cache/sentiment_model` (17 files including `model.safetensors`, `config.json`, `vocab.txt`).\n\n**2–4. Flask API running** — `/app/app.py` serves `POST /sentiment` on `0.0.0.0:5000` using the local model (no network needed at inference time).\n\n**5. Running in background** — started via `nohup python3 app.py &` (PID 114), logging to `/app/service.log`.\n\nVerified behavior:\n- Positive text → `200 {\"sentiment\": \"positive\", \"confidence\": {\"positive\": 0.9999, \"negative\": 0.0001}}`\n- Negative text → `200 {\"sentiment\": \"negative\", \"confidence\": {...}}`\n- Missing `text` / non-string `text` / empty `text` / non-JSON body → `400 {\"error\": \"<message>\"}`\n- Reachable on the container's external IP (0.0.0.0 binding confirmed)","source":{"event_id":"event-0012","field":"thought"}}]

